WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very, very happy
you're here.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:02.836 line:92%
I want to talk about the show.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I want to start by talk--
World Cup time.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.039 size:84% position:42% line:92%
England plays tomorrow.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're already through
to the next round.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will you watch that game,
though?

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.643 line:92%
Is that very important to you?

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes, yes, yes, yes.
-Okay.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I will watch it,
touchingly,

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:18.118
with the same eight friends I've
been watching the World Cup with

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
since 1982.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, fantastic.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does that mean you have to get
to a plane to go see them?

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:23.723 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Or are they coming here?

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.259
-No, no, they come to my house.
-Okay.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.794 line:92%
-And we watch it on the TV.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.062 line:92%
And we -- nothing changes.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're now in
our mid to late 50s.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some of my friends are now
judges and heads of banks

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.102 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and things like that.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.070 line:92%
But we still, if England score,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
we still have
what we call a bundle.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:39.739 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Do you have bundles?

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I -- I don't know.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.307 line:92%
-Well, it just means you all --

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
you all jump on top of
each other.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, like a pig pile
we would call it.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A pig pile, yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course,
your name makes it classier.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we have to do it
quite slowly now

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.384 line:92%
because we've all got bad backs.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right.
-Yeah.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:53.920 line:92%
-So, there's a little bit --

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.156
and I'm sure there's someone
who has certain medical reasons.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
They can't be at the bottom of
bundle anymore.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:00:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, no.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's always one
who is at the bottom,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:01.795 line:92%
because we sort of hate him.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:07.100
So, now -- I feel like there
wasn't a ton of optimism about

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
the English team
going into the World Cup,

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they've won
the first two matches.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you -- Are you falling for
it again?

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:17.010
-We have beaten the footballing
giants of Tunisia and Panama.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the English press
is now saying

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is our year
for the World Cup.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are a bit --
It is, like, it's recidivism.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
That every -- You just keep
falling for the team

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.122 size:75% position:38% line:92%
every year and hope.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is --
I mean, it's been since '82.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, not --
not much has gone right.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.494 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Uh, no. Nothing at all.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Nothing at all.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.597 line:92%
Except, almost every time,

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.799 size:84% position:42%
we lose to the Germans,
and we can't this year.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:42.001 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, there you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's something
to look forward to.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.538 line:92%
I'm so sorry for the Germans.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.341
-You do. You look -- There's a
sadness in this coming through.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.275 line:92%
-Yes, it's breaking my heart.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.711 size:81% position:41%
-When you were young,
you actually worked at

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.948
the Fulham Football Club,
which is a London club.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.151 line:92%
I used to wash the seats there.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.652 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Disgusting job, really.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
And dangerous too,
because for some reason,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.558 line:92%
my work mate was a psychopath.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:06.926 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I said to our boss,

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:10.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't think this guy's very
well, you know, mentally."

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.133 size:84% position:42%
And he said, "Nonsense,
nonsense. He's fine."

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after three weeks,
he stabbed me.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Yes.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience ohs ]

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.139 line:92%
I have to say I resigned.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:19.639 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:22.175 size:88% position:44%
-They let him stay on?
-Oh, yeah. He stayed on.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But that's English football.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:25.445 line:92%
-You're right, exactly there.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's got a go-getter attitude
you don't have.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.382 line:92%
Like, he brought the knife.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, quite.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.218 line:92%
He was the real deal, I was --

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've been a fan of yours
for a long time.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
People have told me
that we look alike.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a little similarity,
and I --

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:39.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Like droopy eyes.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
We got that nice droopy eye.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really --
I will be honest.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the mid-'90s,
I really leaned into the fact

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we looked alike.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had a hairstyle
that I thought --

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.906
I was like, "That looks great on
Hugh Grant's face.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm close enough.
I'm gonna give it a shot."

00:02:55.742 --> 00:03:00.380 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's, like,
that's, like, pretty...

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.918 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very ashamed of this one
because this one,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
you looked great and I did
another terrible thing

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:10.557 line:92%
that you avoided in the '90s,

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.825
which is I grew a terrible thing
on my chin.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the one
I feel ashamed for.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's awful.
We look like two telephones.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:22.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this is based on
a true story.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-The show.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.204 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And tell us a little bit
about Jeremy Thorpe.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.709
-Well, it was this massive
scandal in Britain in the '70s.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.879
I remember it 'cause I, you
know, I was in my teens then.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was just the biggest
political scandal

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:36.449 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you've ever had.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it resulted in
this massive trial,

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.652 line:92%
the trial of the century.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was this guy
who was the head of

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.457
one of our three big parties --
political parties.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolute member of
the establishment.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:49.629
He went to Eaton, you know,
where the royal family go.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.263 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Went to Oxford.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Beautifully dressed.
Very smooth.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:52.832 line:92%
Had a family. Had a wife.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:56.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
It turned out he put a hit on
his ex-gay lover

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was stalking him
and threatening to reveal him.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.507 line:92%
And it was a really crap hit.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- That was
the very English bit.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was so kind of
hopeless and amateurish.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:10.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the hit man was
an out-of-work airline pilot

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.753 size:81% position:41%
who got it all wrong
and used the wrong gun

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
and shot the dog
instead of the man.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:17.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.259 line:92%
So it was very scandalous.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:24.364
And it -- So the series is
quite dark, but also funny

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.198 line:92%
because it was just so absurd.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:28.101
-Well, I will say the -- when I
heard the description of it,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
well, you know,
there's a murder trial

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.004 line:92%
and it's a closeted politician.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.706
And, I think, in this fraught
political time we live in,

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just assumed it would be
so much darker.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is --
It's a weird thing to say.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.612 line:92%
It is a lot of fun as well,

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:43.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a nice thing to watch
about politics right now.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.017 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:45.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's right.
That's right.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they are freaks.
I mean, I --

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:48.855 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:51.524
I've spent the last six years of
my life, very unlike me,

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting heavily involved in
politics in Britain.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
This campaign I've been doing
about evil newspapers.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.366
So I'm up close with politicians
all the time,

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's unquestionably true
that they are weirdos.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who would go into that job?
-Yeah.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.309 line:92%
-You're not paid very much.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, really, with that whole
thing, it's true.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is show business
for the ugly.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.982 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
Narcissistic, egomaniacal.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sociopathic.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.488 size:81% position:41%
And with absolutely --
and very, very rarely

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
any interest in the country
or its welfare, I find.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, you -- so, I mean,
one of the things,

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you've been advocating
for is trying to stop --

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was the hacking scandal
with newspapers.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:32.865 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:33.700 line:92%
-And do you at least find that

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you talk to politicians
about that,

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they are listening to you
and hearing?

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.772
Or do you feel like it's going
in one ear and out the other?

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, they listen
and they are on our side.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
Completely on our side,
actually.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.012 line:92%
I don't think I've ever met one

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is really
philosophically opposed.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's not how politics
works.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's one of the things
that's made me so cynical.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because these big newspapers
are so powerful,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
they make or break
our politicians.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
They choose our prime minister
effectively.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when it comes to
these big votes on --

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:03.429
well, let's have a new system of
regulation where, actually,

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:04.864 line:92%
newspapers do have to, kind of,

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
print the truth
instead of a lie.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:09.068
At the last moment, the
government will always back out,

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:13.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they have to please
these big tax-dodging bastards

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:14.374 size:81% position:41% line:92%
who run the newspaper.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.041 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It's very terrifying.

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:18.945
And I'm glad we don't have any
problems like that over here.

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:19.645 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you don't have
those problems.

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we don't have those.
It's true.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:25.284 line:92%
-No, your press is rather nice.

